{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "quarter-ice-perpetual-cycle",
  "title": "Quarter Ice Perpetual Cycle",
  "description": "A quarter-ice drill to work on both the high cycle and the low cycle, a modification of the Perpetual Cycle drill for smaller spaces or groups too large to keep everyone moving in the original. One line of skaters. The first half is the high cycle, up along the side boards, and the second half the low cycle, behind the net. P1 dumps the puck in to the bottom corner, goes down to retrieve it and walks it along the bottom boards. P2 swings down behind the net, following a bit behind. P1 bounces the puck off the boards and back, and P2 picks it up. P1 continues around the circle and attacks the net, turning toward it as the pass arrives; P2 takes a few steps and passes to P1, who shoots. Then P2 curves back the way they came and goes behind the net to the top of the net to pick up the puck P3 dumped there, and does a quick bump pass off the boards to the corner below the net, where P3 has circled over to. P3 circles up behind the net while P2 curls over toward the front of the net; P3 passes to P2, who shoots. The drill repeats.",
  "tags": [
    "cycle",
    "passing",
    "shooting",
    "offence"
  ],
  "rink": "half-right",
